ByZBYaCXUvdJ7Ifyh60pCHJ-koSu6z2fpkMFtOAZbg37BguWU6Y7Iezj-yNakqChtetD4hl8OR3obo6bwxU-FaIZKcphelgBaHL_E-RR4VS2rCFH7K9MsneN_Gt4Uh79NG7wnKaOKG7tFsZjW4-q-p4uOml1wfIgYH8WhsVBwcU9scBOW4FLarv3W_V6N_sNK8JUEdfUSjgwWGIHVGGQIjKVfV5bE_GGLwf_OKRChjiR0_HXSiwwN4Ye6FmLYVUxiqluys445niOnbMjzZJPsGctF-RFNcipxe0BHZxWKTegHxN5q9guGVG_baXUpsn6tQTfST6S5D9njftFC0t-K1bvf5ss-hK1g6q5AnMjswUZwGxf_celDykD6XIPVbJ96iaMrCxEXUrav0eE1G9oOlaFVJNp1HUmpAGmi2Brj5aZrM6bb2k_xY8Pb6vcftltNoHKpHldRXERNrr1wVgYn9-aDhSpvGr6Hh69v3iZQtzKxKPuDLcUKsVXiVGula4t1Yn3iwO2OWtqp8yIqUN8EbRMok3Os4CJ3e6UzUTUyBgHxYdWN2lWVGve2yHdMg11m3rSKQBBFlGUJNT5xwc_Kw0rrNEfpTMB8MkSjKprUwCswJYCBzN3gfdEwsMtjtf8WcRlMTQ5MTnwomb_ui4hNBW12SD4dO4L1HlQZyTAsdqaLyQJ_yKFgX0qg3g8VQSZ2c9BIZVI4pi2u6bHk7ZqW8sH-jWZXw=="},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_01f47fbc4914fd27016adb42053e0481918fee6e115745142f","call_id":"call_b3d6dc4f56304e7bb3a6cb62c16985c6","name":"submit_draft","arguments":"{\"artifact\":{\"base_input\":\"prior-candidate.json\",\"patches\":[{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/33/type\",\"value\":\"Q-dimension of Q tensor_R N for a finitely generated torsion-free R-module N\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/33/declaration\",\"value\":\"For any finitely generated torsion-free R-module N, define rank_R(N)=dim_Q(Q tensor_R N), where Q=Frac(R); this definition does not presuppose that N is free.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/2/text\",\"value\":\"For each i set J_i={c in C: c e_i is in M_R}. First, M_R is finite free over R: if m_1,...,m_n is the original Z-basis of M, then 1 tensor m_1,...,1 tensor m_n is an R-basis of R tensor_Z M, since the Z-coordinate isomorphism M≅Z^n extends to the explicit isomorphism R tensor_Z M≅R^n. The image E_i,i(M_R)=J_i e_i is finitely generated over R: it is the image of this finite module under the R-linear projection E_i,i. It is nonzero because M_R spans V(lambda) over C and E_i,i is a nonzero projection. Since E_i,j preserves M_R, applying it to c e_j proves J_j subset J_i; reversing i,j proves equality. Denote the common module by J. The coordinate projections give the internal direct sum M_R=⊕_{i=0}^{lambda} J e_i: each vector has its unique e-coordinate expansion, and its i-th coordinate belongs to J_i by the definition of J_i. Thus J is finitely generated (as just shown) and torsion-free, since it is an R-submodule of the field C and R is a domain. We now compute scalar-extension dimension before using any rank-one or ideal conclusion. Let Q=Frac(R), and let ι:Q tensor_R M_R→Q^n be the isomorphism obtained by extending the displayed original-basis coordinate isomorphism R tensor_Z M≅R^n; hence dim_Q(Q tensor_R M_R)=n. Tensor the coordinate direct-sum isomorphism with Q. The explicit compatible isomorphism ⊕_{i=0}^{lambda}(Q tensor_R J)→Q tensor_R M_R sends the i-th summand element q tensor c to q tensor(c e_i); its inverse is induced by the coordinate projections onto J e_i followed by e_i-coordinate extraction. Consequently, writing d=dim_Q(Q tensor_R J), finite because J is finitely generated, dimensions give n=(lambda+1)d=nd. Since n=lambda+1 is a positive integer, d=1. In particular the scalar-extension map μ:Q tensor_R J→C, q tensor c↦qc, is injective: Q tensor_R J is the localization of the R-submodule J⊂C, and an element maps to zero only if some nonzero denominator multiplier annihilates an element of J, which torsion-freeness forbids. Its image is nonzero (J is nonzero) and one-dimensional over Q, so choosing any nonzero image element identifies Q tensor_R J with Q as a Q-vector space. This proves the rank-one identification without assuming J free. Now use μ to regard J as a nonzero finitely generated R-submodule of Q. Clear denominators in a finite generating set to obtain a nonzero finitely generated ideal I of R with I=d_0J for some nonzero d_0 in R. Every nonzero q in Q is p^k u for an integer k and a unit u in R; among a finite set of nonzero generators of I choose the least exponent k. Every generator is in p^k R and one is p^k times a unit, so I=p^k R. Hence J is free of rank one. For a generator a of J, the vectors a e_i form an R-basis of M_R by the direct-sum decomposition.\"}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"d85a26d2-b3d1-467b-ad99-347d343ed200","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":37246,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1269,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":369},"total_tokens":38515,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_01f47fbc4914fd27016adb41c1d12481919900d48159fdda44":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_01f47fbc4914fd27016adb41c5ad908191a8907f9444ddeef6":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_01f47fbc4914fd27016adb41c7888881919cd17ad611e3749c":{"input_tokens":34,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_01f47fbc4914fd27016adb41cad1948191873cf8a006654637":{"input_tokens":33,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_01f47fbc4914fd27016adb41cd6e04819190b592862a1ca86e":{"input_tokens":35,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_01f47fb